  "source_qa_workflow": {
    "id": "XevQwFviJHUobw0U",
    "name": "QA - Ingress Round Trip"
  },
  "description": "The same provider_message_id redelivered with a different body is an IDEMPOTENCY_CONFLICT that requires human review and permits no mutation.",
  "why_it_exists": "A provider message id is only as trustworthy as the provider. If the same id arrives carrying different content, one of the two is wrong and silently overwriting the stored legal communication would destroy the record. The QA fixture deliberately flips the body to a liability denial to make the stakes concrete.",
